# Secrets
cabinet/.env
.oauth-backup-*.json

# Built Apple Calendar helper binary (arch-specific, signed at install via
# cabinet/scripts/build-calendar-helper.sh; source lives in
# framework/frontdoor/calread_helper/)
/bin/cabinet-calread

# Built menu-bar companion bundle (arch-specific, assembled + ad-hoc-signed
# on-target via cabinet/scripts/build-companion.sh; source lives in
# cabinet/companion/ — the bundle must never enter git or the egg)
/bin/Cabinet Companion.app/

# Claude Code auto-memory (per-developer, not part of the framework)
.claude/memory/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Local settings layer (Claude Code convention: per-machine, never committed).
# On the live box it carries the AUD-2 model-fallback-pager Notification hook
# (germline .claude/settings.json is schg-locked — see
# docs/proposals/germline-addendum-claude-code-audit-2026-07-07.md §AUD-2).
.claude/settings.local.json

# Agent definitions at .claude/agents/ are derived by the preset loader
# (copied from presets/<active>/agents/ with instance/agents/ overlays).
# Source of truth lives in presets/ and instance/agents/ — do NOT track
# the derived copies.
.claude/agents/*.md
!.claude/agents/.gitkeep
# Loader-generated markers + drift backups for the load-preset clobber guard
# (audit finding #5, 2026-07-07): .<slug>.md.gen.sha records what the loader
# last wrote; <slug>.md.clobbered-backup preserves refused hand-edited copies.
.claude/agents/.*.gen.sha
.claude/agents/*.clobbered-backup

# Officer-skill overlays (egg plan R090): cabinet/officer-skills/ ships only
# generic role files; deployment-specific skill refreshes live in
# instance/officer-skills/ and are materialized as untracked symlinks at the
# fixed path the germline post-compact hook reads (see
# instance/officer-skills/README.md). Do NOT re-track the materialized links.
cabinet/officer-skills/cos.txt
cabinet/officer-skills/comms-officer.txt
cabinet/officer-skills/*-ceo.txt

# Runtime Cabinet state assembled by cabinet/scripts/load-preset.sh
# Derived from framework/ + presets/<active>/ + instance/ on each start.
# Do not commit.

# Per-officer working directories (created at runtime for session isolation)
officers/
# Exception: CoS MCP config registers the host MCP server — ship with framework
# so every Cabinet install wires host access to CoS on boot. No secrets in file.
!officers/cos/
!officers/cos/.mcp.json

# Runtime logs
memory/logs/*.jsonl
memory/logs/*.log

# Hook-regression runner outputs (overwritten on every run-hook-regression.sh)
cabinet/tests/hook-regression/.last-run/

# Per-officer session state (resets between runs)
instance/memory/tier2/**/.session-state.json

# Durable role state — seeded by cabinet/scripts/bootstrap-roles.sh on
# first deployment (called from setup-mac.sh Step 5.5). Source of truth
# is the script + presets/<active>/agents/. Do NOT commit the per-
# deployment seeded YAML — they encode product_slug + auth level chosen
# at activation time.
instance/roles/active/*.yml
instance/roles/archive/*.yml
instance/roles/hats/*.yml
!instance/roles/active/.gitkeep
!instance/roles/archive/.gitkeep
!instance/roles/hats/.gitkeep

# Build artifacts
cabinet/dashboard/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
cabinet/dashboard/.next/

# ============================================================
# Runtime state (layer 3 — product-specific, evolves on server)
# Protected from git pull overwriting server evolution.
# Foundation files (layer 2) are git-tracked and safe to update.
# ============================================================

# Product config (each deployment has its own)
instance/config/product.yml

# Deployment-local: which project is active on THIS machine (activate-project.sh rewrites it)
instance/config/active-project.txt
# Deployment-local: which preset is active on THIS machine (tracked template: active-preset.example)
instance/config/active-preset
# Deployment-local: roster seed for bootstrap-roles.sh --roster (generated by cabinet-init)
instance/config/roster.yml
# Deployment-local (2026-07-17): the Captain's comms-charter override + its
# amendments ledger — written at RUNTIME by framework.attention.charter.amend
# (first shipped writer: the cabinet-init quiet-hours question). Captain-
# specific routing/quiet-hours rulings never enter the universal repo; the
# tracked default is framework/attention/charter-default.yml.
instance/config/comms-charter.yml
instance/config/comms-charter-amendments.jsonl
# Deployment-local (product/captain-agnostic foundation, 2026-07-14): the
# concrete war-room census seed list — real product/personal items belong
# here, never in the tracked seed-war-room.py (tracked twin: war-room-seed.yml.example)
instance/config/war-room-seed.yml
# Deployment-local (R166): the captain-specific publish-scan pattern suite —
# real name/employer/product literals live ONLY here (tracked synthetic
# template: publish-scan-patterns.local.example); egg-publish-gate.sh +
# cabinet-feedback.sh fail closed without it on a private-side checkout
instance/config/publish-scan-patterns.local
# Deployment-local: lane-CEO role defs rendered from the portfolio template
instance/agents/*-ceo.md

# R091: per-officer self-wake prompts are instance materializations rendered
# from cabinet/loop-prompts/_template.txt ({{officer}} slots). Only the
# template + the generic Chair prompt ship; lane prompts live on disk
# untracked (canonical copies in instance/loop-prompts/, also untracked).
cabinet/loop-prompts/*.txt
!cabinet/loop-prompts/_template.txt
!cabinet/loop-prompts/cos.txt
instance/loop-prompts/

# Officer working notes (accumulated at runtime)
instance/memory/tier2/**/*.md
!instance/memory/tier2/**/.gitkeep

# Day-1 synthetic runtime artifacts (hatch-seeded local renders — a careless
# `git add` must never commit them)
instance/memory/demo-receipt.md
instance/memory/first-briefing-*.md

# Runtime archives (migration snapshots, etc.)
instance/archive/

# Runtime state + briefing renders (materialized by running services)
instance/state/
instance/cache/
instance/memory/briefings/

# Formation runs (Phase 3): per-run journals, IOU artifacts, flight logs,
# and their _pre-adopt undo archives — runtime data, never committed
instance/onboarding/formation/
instance/onboarding/v2/
instance/onboarding/purge-receipts/
instance/onboarding/.onboarding-v2.lock
# Universal Evidence Recorder v1 store: local Captain-owned ledgers, signing
# key, controls, receipts, and explicit exports never enter git.
instance/evidence/

# Experience records, decision log, research archive
memory/tier3/

# Evolved skills (created/modified by the learning loop at runtime)
memory/skills/evolved/**/*.md
!memory/skills/evolved/.gitkeep

# Shared interface content (populated by officers at runtime)
shared/interfaces/**/*.md
!shared/interfaces/**/.gitkeep

# Deployment-specific plans (not part of the generic framework)
founders-cabinet-plan.md

# Node
node_modules/

# Python bytecode caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docker volumes (managed by Docker, not git)
pgdata/
redisdata/

# Secrets dir (CRO + officer secret-routing per FW-018 Phase B chgrp pattern)
secrets/

# Hook FP-rate logs (Spec 043 — runtime data, per-cabinet, never sync)
cabinet/logs/*
!cabinet/logs/.gitkeep

# Hook cache (Spec 046 voice transcripts; future caches per hook spec)
cabinet/cache/*
!cabinet/cache/.gitkeep

# Deployment-specific extension choices (templates are .example, tracked).
# Each deployment activates its own — keep the universal product clean.
instance/config/extensions.yml
instance/config/required-plugins.yml
instance/config/extra-mcps.json
.claude/project-config.json
instance/config/autonomy.yml
cabinet/launchd/generated/

# runtime artifacts (written by falsifier-daily / act-first flag) — never commit
shared/interfaces/falsifier-series.jsonl
shared/interfaces/envelope-violations.jsonl
instance/config/act-first-enabled

# Learning-loop + eval runtime series (written by running lanes/daemons —
# same class as falsifier-series; never commit)
shared/interfaces/action-lessons.yml
shared/interfaces/charter-shadow-series.jsonl
shared/interfaces/golden-eval-scalar.jsonl
shared/interfaces/memory-supersession-proposals.jsonl
shared/interfaces/memory-supersession-soak.jsonl
shared/interfaces/needs-ledger.jsonl
shared/interfaces/prediction-calibration.jsonl
shared/interfaces/preference-pairs.jsonl
# workaround-retirement proposals (needs-ledger pattern) — appended by
# cabinet/scripts/workaround-retest.py on fix_confirmed verdicts; never commit
shared/interfaces/workaround-retire-proposals.jsonl

# Weekly governance-review label digests (evidence Phase 3, RAMP-2 ritual) —
# content-free per-label lines + session markers appended by
# cabinet/scripts/governance-review.py; Captain-owned runtime data, anchored
# off-box daily (evidence-anchor.py), never committed. Session transcripts
# land in shared/interfaces/governance-reviews/*.md, already covered by the
# shared/interfaces/**/*.md rule above.
shared/interfaces/governance-labels.jsonl

# Phase-4 shadow-detector findings journal (evidence Phase 4, shadow law) —
# one JSON line per run appended by cabinet/scripts/evidence-shadow-detectors.py
# (staged dark); Captain-facing runtime series, never committed
shared/interfaces/evidence-shadow-findings.jsonl

# Cabinet World runtime read-model outputs (world-census E0a / world-chronicle
# E0b — append-only replay history; instance data, never committed)
shared/interfaces/world-chronicle.jsonl
shared/interfaces/world/

# War-room census artifact (attention queue.write_artifacts — rewritten each
# 300s surface drain; PII-scrubbed runtime projection, never committed)
shared/interfaces/attention-queue.json

# Cabinet World assets (E1): LimeZu packs are commercial-licensed — binaries
# NEVER committed. Only the content-addressed manifest is tracked; every
# asset must pass cabinet/scripts/world-asset-gate.py before the renderer
# may load it (WORLD-E1-ASSETS).
cabinet/dashboard/public/world-assets/*
!cabinet/dashboard/public/world-assets/manifest.json
# …EXCEPT owned commissioned originals (world-asset-intake.py --promote;
# license "owned — org-original"): org-owned art IS committable — only the
# LimeZu commercial binaries stay ignored.
!cabinet/dashboard/public/world-assets/originals/

# World-aesthetic calibration corpus: LimeZu-derived showcase scenes +
# Captain-rejected build screenshots are licensed/instance data — images
# never committed; only build_corpus.py + the sha256 manifest are tracked.
cabinet/scripts/world-aesthetic/corpus/*
!cabinet/scripts/world-aesthetic/corpus/manifest.json

# Vision-judge golden frames (Captain-approved renders are LimeZu-derived,
# licensed — same rule as the corpus above): only the sha256 + per-region
# threshold manifest is tracked. Judge run bundles (blinded staged corpus
# copies + agent results) are ephemeral judgment artifacts, never committed.
cabinet/scripts/world-aesthetic/goldens/*
!cabinet/scripts/world-aesthetic/goldens/manifest.json
cabinet/scripts/world-aesthetic/judge/runs/

# Library retirement (2026-07-16): retire-library-export.py writes DB-derived
# officer/instance knowledge here — runtime-only, NEVER committed (product-
# brain/ is tracked and ships in the public egg; the archive must not).
# Both candidate roots covered: pre- and post-vault-rename trees.
product-brain/library-archive/
vault/library-archive/
